Namespace       ->  root\cimv2
Class           ->  Win32 Process
Properties ->       Caption ~ The process name
                    Command Line ~ Name and arguments

Methods         ->  Create() ~ Spawn a new process
                    Terminate() ~ Kill a process

WMI Classes belong to a particular namespace
WmiMgmt.msc enumerates them
Most commonly used is root\cimv2
Classes provide an object-oriented interface to hardware/software via:
Properties (data)
Methods (functions that do something)
One example of malware behavior using Win32_process: Enumerate processes, compare the name to
something like procexp or procmon to evade analysis, and terminate those of interest.


WMI Classes and MSDN
